  "implementation": {
    "projection": "Original q_b/kv_a/o E4 codes plus F32 block128 scales enter the existing canonical importer and dynamic A128 Divide/floor1e-10 projection. Actual BF16 input and output boundaries remain explicit.",
    "absorption": "One original BF16 kv_b[32768,512] supplies both per-head key/value matrices. One ordinary cold Graph prepares dense BF16 layouts, shared by all hot recipes. The original device kv_b source retires after preparation; no whole F32 weight shadow or hot per-head repacking.",
    "attention": "64 heads, NoPE256, latent512, value256, no RoPE; scale remains1/16. Existing selected IDs and compact CKV Gather/SDPA stay shared. The F32 cache carrier stores exact widening of actual BF16 latent rows, not unrounded F32 values; actual attention return stores BF16 before value absorption.",
    "residual": "Post-attention norm uses the actual F32 EH+O sum and original BF16 gamma. The separate residual return stores BF16 for subsequent FFN addition; the norm does not consume a prematurely rounded residual.",
    "state": "The same complete state store, one atomic Head, accepted prefixes0/1/2, target bonus policy, epoch seed, indexer skip, journal/direct catchup, full-vocabulary greedy feedback and old readonly results remain."
